# Project core

Static Next.js on S3/CloudFront; Cognito via Amplify in the browser. Terraform
for all AWS; GitHub Actions + OIDC deploy (no long-lived AWS keys in CI).

| Environment | Branch   | Terraform root        |
|-------------|----------|------------------------|
| dev         | dev      | infra/envs/dev         |
| staging     | staging  | infra/envs/staging     |
| prod        | main     | infra/envs/prod        |

## Folder boundaries

- `frontend/` — UI and client-only app logic (static export).
- `backend/` — server-side app logic when added (API, workers).
- `infra/` — Terraform only; no app logic in provisioners or inline Lambda.
- Fix app bugs in app code; never patch around them in `.tf` files.

Secrets: Cognito pool/client IDs are public build-time values; everything else
in GitHub env secrets or local gitignored tfvars. No identifying values in git.

Bootstrap (`infra/bootstrap`) is manual and separate from deploy workflows.

## Scoped rules

Detailed standards load from `.cursor/rules/` by path:

- `frontend.mdc` → `frontend/**`
- `backend.mdc` → `backend/**`
- `infra.mdc` → `infra/**`

Long-form reference (optional): root `CLAUDE.md`.

## Commits

`feat(infra|frontend|backend):`, `fix(...)`, `chore(ci):`, etc.
